  <text>
    <body>
      <p>George Zeplin, professor of music, is listed in <ref target="civic?id=Queensberry%20Street">Queensberry Street</ref> in the Sands &amp; McDougall directories from 1860 to 1862, at No. 40 in 1860 and No. 34 in 1861 and 1862. He is in the teachers' table on the <ref target="civic?id=Schools">Schools</ref> page.</p>
      <p>From 1868 the directories list G. F. Zeplin, musician, in Queensberry Street (No. 19 in 1870), and in <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> at No. 74 in 1868. From 1871 G. F. Zeplin is listed as a draper: at 49 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> in 1871, at 19 Queensberry Street, the musician's number, in 1872 and 1873, and at 27 Madeline Street in 1874. A Mrs Zeplin, draper, is listed in Queensberry and Bouverie streets from 1868 to 1870.</p>
      <p>A Frederick Zeplin is named in the <ref target="civic?id=Seven%20Stars%20hotel">Seven Stars hotel</ref> entry, as the hotel's licensee in the 1880s and 1900s. Whether he is the same man is not known.</p>
      <p><hi rend="italic">This entry is a machine-assisted first draft by Common Ground, written from the directory records. Please correct or add to it.</hi></p>
